# Response headers for every page on the public origin, imported by Caddyfile.
#
# A field with a leading "?" is only a default: it is written when the upstream
# did not send that header itself, so the stricter policy Keycloak sends with
# its own login pages stands. Each default is a directive of its own, because
# within one header block Caddy writes the "?" fields only when the upstream
# sent none of them.

# The origin is only ever served over HTTPS; Caddy redirects port 80.
header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
# Only this origin may frame its pages, so Pay and Reserve can't be clickjacked
# from someone else's site.
header ?Content-Security-Policy "frame-ancestors 'self'"
header ?X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
header ?Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
